cff-version: 1.2.0
type: software
message: >-
  If you use Homo spatialis in research, please cite this software and state the
  version, data pack, configuration and planner used. This is a scholarly citation
  request, not an additional condition of the Apache-2.0 license.
title: "Homo spatialis · LLMs Becoming Us"
authors:
  - family-names: Liu
    given-names: Chengyu
    website: "https://github.com/lcy432"
version: "0.1.0"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/lcy432/homo-spatialis"
url: "https://github.com/lcy432/homo-spatialis"
abstract: >-
  An exploratory spatial life simulation engine that separates agent planning
  from explicit monthly economic settlement and outcome-based evaluation.
  The reproducible baseline uses synthetic people and cities with a deterministic
  mock planner. It does not establish predictive validity for real cities or
  individual life outcomes. The repository includes a methods report and
  contribution and data provenance guidelines.
keywords:
  - spatial welfare
  - life simulation
  - agent-based modeling
  - research software
  - reproducibility
